  "notes": "Source: official USC 'Major Map: Computer Science' for the Bachelor of Science in Computer Science (B.S.C.S.), Molinaroli College of Engineering and Computing, Department of Computer Science & Engineering, Bulletin Year 2026-2027: https://itunesu.sc.edu/about/offices_and_divisions/advising/documents/major_maps/2026-2027/2026_cs_map.pdf . Transcription method: manual transcription of every semester row (course subject/title, credit hours, prerequisites, notes) from the official major map PDF on 2026-09-30. Term names use the map's own 'Semester One' ... 'Semester Eight' numbering. Student-choice slots (choice:true) cover the Carolina Core requirements (AIU, SCI, CMS, GSS, GFL, GHS), the Laboratory Science Requirement (any 4-credit CC-SCI lab science), CSCE Major Electives (any CSCE course 500 or higher; a 12-hour AI or Cybersecurity concentration may replace them per map note), and free electives (4-13 hours per map note). The ENGL 462 / ENGL 463 alternative is a choice slot with both options named. Prerequisites follow the map; where the map lists alternative entry paths (e.g. CSCE 106 instead of CSCE 145, MATH 174/574 instead of MATH 374, MATH 544 instead of MATH 344), the prereq array uses the course on this plan's path and the alternative is listed in external_prereqs. Minimum-grade and '* included in CS program GPA' markers from the map are not modeled in the schema. Caveats: (a) map notes say students who place into MATH 115 must complete it before MATH 141; (b) GFL requirement: proficiency equivalent to the 121 course (placement score 2+, or 109+110 in FREN/GERM/LATN/SPAN, or 121 in another language) -- students who do not place out may need additional hours; (c) CSCE 490 is fall only, CSCE 492 is spring only, CSCE 330 is fall only; (d) all undergraduates must complete a 3-credit founding-documents course, which may overlap a requirement (see Bulletin); (e) last 25% of degree must be completed in residence; (f) the major map is a recommended sequence -- the map's disclaimer advises consulting an academic advisor. Graduation Requirements Summary on the map: 120 total hours, 30 major, 46-55 college & program, 35-41 Carolina Core, 2.00 institutional GPA.",
